Line 2: An "unless" needs yes or no to decide, but this is a number.
    unless total:
           ^^^^^
Compare it with something, like "unless x is 5".

Line 4: "stop here" only works inside a function.
    stop here if total is 5.
    ^^^^^^^^^
It ends the function and goes back to whoever used it. To end the whole program, write "stop the program".

Line 6: "double" gives back a value, so it can't stop without one here.
        stop here if x is 0.
        ^^^^^^^^^
Give back a value here too, like "give back 0".

Line 9: "give back" only works inside a function.
    give back 1 unless total is 5.
    ^^^^^^^^^^^
It ends a function and hands a value back to whoever called it. To end the whole program, write "stop the program".
